w: 1.~We praise thee, O God, our Re- deem- er, Cre- a- tor, In grate- ful de- vo- tion our tri- bute we bring. We lay it be- fore thee, we kneel _ and a- dore thee, We bless thy ho- ly name, _ glad prais- es we sing.
w: 2.~We wor- ship thee, God of our fa- thers, we bless thee; Through life's storm and tem- pest our guide hast thou been. When pe- rils o'er- take us, es- cape _ thou wilt make us, And with thy help, O Lord, _ our bat- tles we win.
w: 3.~With voi- ces u- ni- ted our prais- es we of- fer, To thee, great Je- ho- vah, glad an- thems we raise. Thy strong arm will guide us, our God _ is be- side us, To thee, our great Re- deem- _ er, for ever be praise.
